text:
elaine: quick design sync 11 proposing a denser credentials row to surface more keys per page. thinking: visible Rotate button, move Revoke into kebab/overflow. concerns: destructive affordance, mobile tap targets, and how we announce secret copy. screenshot: https://img.redwood/mock/dense-cred-rows.png

josh: ok with denser rows if we preserve keyboard focus visibility. agree Rotate should be the primary action. put Revoke in kebab to reduce accidental clicks.

sasha: UX nits: if we compress rows, bump vertical spacing a few px so focus rings don't collide. ensure interactive areas stay >=44px on touch. empty state: center the primary Create key CTA and add short explanation copy.

kevin: a11y notes: toasts should use aria-live="polite" by default. For clipboard success, polite is good; for failure use aria-live="assertive" so SRs catch it. revoke confirmation should use role="alertdialog" and trap focus. add aria-describedby on the final Revoke to link to the warning text.

elaine: good call. also thinking about soft-undo window for revokes. support tickets request longer windows sometimes. ops, any constraints?

ops-kate: from ops: we mark keys disabled immediately in metadata, but keep them accepted for a short grace period for in-flight requests. current infra accommodates 30s without extra complexity; 60s is possible but will change monitoring/metrics assumptions.

josh: propose default 30s undo, org-configurable up to 60s. UI should clearly show undo availability: toast with countdown or microcopy on the revoke action: "Revoke (undo available for 30s)" or a tooltip.

sasha: timeline detail: toast text should be concise: "Key revoked 1 undo available for 30s" (or similar). avoid long sentences.

aria-bot: accessibility-check: recommend aria-live="polite" on the toast container. For the revoke flow, ensure initial focus goes to the dialog heading and that the destructive button has aria-describedby="revoke-warning". Add accessible name to kebab menu button.

elaine: implementing defaults: 30s undo, admin page can change to 60s. moving Revoke to overflow, Rotate visible primary. will increase row height + maintain 44px targets. I'll update mocks and add copy edits.

elaine: quick clipboard snippet for the spec (keeps SR friendly toasts):
```html
<button id="reveal-secret">Show secret</button>
<div id="toast" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></div>
<script>
document.getElementById('reveal-secret').addEventListener('click', ()=>{
  navigator.clipboard.writeText(secret).then(()=>{
    // concise, visible toast
    document.getElementById('toast').textContent = 'Secret copied';
  }, ()=>{
    // make sure screen readers get this
    const err = document.createElement('div');
    err.className = 'sr-only';
    err.setAttribute('aria-live', 'assertive');
    err.textContent = 'Failed to copy secret';
    document.body.appendChild(err);
    document.getElementById('toast').textContent = 'Failed to copy';
  });
});
</script>
```

josh: perfect. add visually-hidden text inside the error path so SRs get assertive announce. keep visible toasts short: "Secret copied" not "Secret copied to clipboard".

sasha: copy tweak: for the revoke dialog warning, prefer active phrasing: "This key will stop working for your apps. You can undo for 30 seconds." instead of passive voice.

elaine: noted. I'll adjust the dialog copy and put the undo timer in the toast. after mocks updated i'll post in #design. thanks! :white_check_mark:
